<main class="shell container-xxl px-3 px-lg-4">
    <section id="resources" class="page-intro">
        <div class="section-heading row g-3 align-items-end">
            <div class="col-lg-7">
                <div class="eyebrow">Next Steps</div>
                <h1>Continue with the right next page, dataset, or entry point</h1>
            </div>
            <div class="col-lg-5">
                <p class="body-copy">
                    Use official data portals when you are ready to work with the archive, or open the studio for a more
                    visual and exploratory understanding first.
                </p>
            </div>
        </div>
        <div class="row g-4 source-grid">
            <div class="col-md-6 col-xl-3">
                <article class="source-card h-100">
                    <h3>USGS EarthExplorer</h3>
                    <p>Search, preview, and download Landsat collections and supporting products.</p>
                    <a class="resource-link" href="https://earthexplorer.usgs.gov/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Open EarthExplorer</a>
                </article>
            </div>
            <div class="col-md-6 col-xl-3">
                <article class="source-card h-100">
                    <h3>USGS Landsat Missions</h3>
                    <p>Mission summaries, product documentation, collection guidance, and distribution details.</p>
                    <a class="resource-link" href="https://www.usgs.gov/landsat-missions" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Open USGS Landsat</a>
                </article>
            </div>
            <div class="col-md-6 col-xl-3">
                <article class="source-card h-100">
                    <h3>NASA HLS</h3>
                    <p>Harmonized Landsat Sentinel-2 overview, methods, product background, and access guidance.</p>
                    <a class="resource-link" href="https://hls.gsfc.nasa.gov/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Open HLS</a>
                </article>
            </div>
            <div class="col-md-6 col-xl-3">
                <article class="source-card h-100">
                    <h3>Interactive Studio</h3>
                    <p>Open orbit, resolution, band, and map-based remote-sensing tools.</p>
                    <a class="resource-link" href="/studio">Open studio</a>
                </article>
            </div>
        </div>
        <div class="section-heading row g-3 align-items-end mt-5">
            <div class="col-lg-7">
                <div class="eyebrow">Images And Video</div>
                <h2>Use source-backed media for tutoring</h2>
            </div>
            <div class="col-lg-5">
                <p class="body-copy">These NASA and USGS resources include high-resolution imagery, animations, captions, transcripts, and public-domain usage guidance where applicable.</p>
            </div>
        </div>
        <div class="media-grid">
            <article class="media-card">
                <img src="https://svs.gsfc.nasa.gov/vis/a000000/a003600/a003632/et.0700_0.jpg" alt="High-resolution Landsat evapotranspiration teaching image">
                <div>
                    <h3>Evapotranspiration image set</h3>
                    <p>3840x2160 visual, thermal, and evapotranspiration frames for explaining water use in irrigated fields.</p>
                    <a class="resource-link" href="https://svs.gsfc.nasa.gov/3632/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Open NASA SVS media</a>
                </div>
            </article>
            <article class="media-card">
                <img src="https://svs.gsfc.nasa.gov/vis/a010000/a014700/a014712/Firewatch_Thumb.png" alt="Guardian Landsat Firewatch video art">
                <div>
                    <h3>Guardian Landsat Firewatch</h3>
                    <p>Video and caption files for teaching fire risk, burn mapping, and ecosystem recovery.</p>
                    <a class="resource-link" href="https://svs.gsfc.nasa.gov/14712/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Open fire video</a>
                </div>
            </article>
            <article class="media-card">
                <img src="https://svs.gsfc.nasa.gov/vis/a010000/a013500/a013543/LandsatAg-Thumbnail.png" alt="NASA Landsat agriculture video thumbnail">
                <div>
                    <h3>Farming data from space</h3>
                    <p>Video, transcript, and irrigation animation resources for crop condition and water-use lessons.</p>
                    <a class="resource-link" href="https://svs.gsfc.nasa.gov/13543/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Open agriculture video</a>
                </div>
            </article>
            <article class="media-card">
                <img src="/img/mss_band_l9.jpg" alt="Landsat band comparison visual">
                <div>
                    <h3>Landsat and HLS time series</h3>
                    <p>Current 2026 gallery of Landsat and HLS animations for flooding, cities, reservoirs, glaciers, agriculture, wetlands, and algal blooms.</p>
                    <a class="resource-link" href="https://svs.gsfc.nasa.gov/15039/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Open time-series gallery</a>
                </div>
            </article>
        </div>
        <div class="section-heading row g-3 align-items-end mt-5">
            <div class="col-lg-7">
                <div class="eyebrow">Official Classrooms</div>
                <h2>Bring in ready-made NASA lessons</h2>
            </div>
            <div class="col-lg-5">
                <p class="body-copy">Use these when a learner needs structured activities rather than another explanation.</p>
            </div>
        </div>
        <div class="recipe-grid">
            <article class="recipe-card"><strong>Landsat at Home</strong><span>Band-combination, GIF, change-over-time, decoder, map matching, and other activities.</span><a class="resource-link" href="https://landsat.gsfc.nasa.gov/outreach/landsat-home/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Open activities</a></article>
            <article class="recipe-card"><strong>NASA STEM Landsat</strong><span>K-14 classroom exercises, data tutorials, fact sheets, imagery, and animations.</span><a class="resource-link" href="https://www.nasa.gov/stem-content/landsat-science-education/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Open NASA STEM page</a></article>
            <article class="recipe-card"><strong>USGS EarthExplorer</strong><span>Search and download Level-1, Level-2, ARD, and supporting Landsat products.</span><a class="resource-link" href="https://earthexplorer.usgs.gov/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Open EarthExplorer</a></article>
            <article class="recipe-card"><strong>Visible Earth Gallery</strong><span>Public-domain Landsat imagery with scientific context and attribution guidance.</span><a class="resource-link" href="https://landsat.visibleearth.nasa.gov/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Open gallery</a></article>
        </div>
        <div class="source-note mt-4">
            <strong>Attribution guidance:</strong> NASA's Landsat multimedia and Visible Earth pages identify Landsat-derived public-domain media and commonly credit imagery as USGS/NASA Landsat or Landsat imagery courtesy of NASA Goddard Space Flight Center and U.S. Geological Survey.
        </div>
        <div class="page-nav">
            <a class="button" href="/briefing/future">Previous: future direction</a>
            <a class="button button-primary" href="/studio">Next: interactive studio</a>
        </div>
    </section>
</main>
